{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And they shall be destroyed</b> — at the shrines of the Baals, on account of the calves." "<b>And they shall say</b> — Rabbi Moses said: that \"they shall say\" is figurative on account of the altars, in the manner of \"for it has heard\" [1 Kings 8:44, i.e. an inanimate object spoken of as hearing], and the meaning is that they shall be seen no more. And Yefet said: Their worshippers shall say, on account of their abundant distress."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:49.186958691Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}